    "about": "Kollur Mookambika Temple is located at Kollur in Byndoor Taluk of Udupi District in the region of Tulunadu ,state of Karnataka, near Kundapur India. It is a Hindu temple dedicated to the mother goddess Mookambika. Mookambika is the union of Adi Parashakti and Parabramha as the Linga has integrated on its left side \"Maha Kali, Maha Lakshmi and Maha Saraswathi\". The temple is very special because it is part of the 108 Durgalayas and 108 Shivalayas."
